# Headers Cloudflare Pages sends with every file of the app.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy here holds only frame-ancestors, the one
# directive a <meta> tag cannot carry. The rest of the policy lives in the
# <meta> at the top of index.html, the single place to edit it: a browser
# enforces both, so a second full copy here could only drift out of step
# and block something the page was meant to allow.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), serial=(), usb=()
